    "narrative": "The slate for May 28th presents a narrow window for Ghost Ride the WHIP, as the bulk of our speed-oriented core\u2014including **Corbin Carroll**, **Jose Caballero**, and the rising **James Wood**\u2014are sidelined by a team-wide off-day. Consequently, **Zach McKinstry** headlines our active roster today with a score of 57.26. While he holds a marginal efficiency rating, his matchup against Rodriguez (4.95 xERA) provides the highest ceiling of our active bats, bolstered by a 19% boost for the favorable pitcher profile. We are also deploying **Austin Riley** (55.38) and **Seiya Suzuki** (44.55); while **Seiya Suzuki** faces a daunting task against the elite stuff of Skenes, his projection is marginally salvaged by favorable wind conditions blowing out at the park.\n\nThe bench remains static today due to the lack of available alternatives, but the decision to keep **Austin Riley** in the starting slot despite a 35% rain risk highlights our commitment to maintaining a full lineup when the schedule is thin. We are monitoring the official card for **Austin Riley** and **Seiya Suzuki** closely, as any shift down the order would compress their efficiency scores further. With the scarcity of stolen bases being our primary league concern, the absence of **Brice Turang**, **Mickey Moniak**, and **Carson Williams** forces us to play for total volume and run production today. We are playing a conservative hand, banking on **Zach McKinstry** to capitalize on a soft opposing arm while waiting for the rest of our roster\u2014including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Alex Freeland**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Cole Young**, **Henry Bolte**, and **Trevor Story**\u2014to return to the field.",
